:: Brian Desk Vent [micro_event event nobr] {"position":"1425,3275","size":"100,100"}
/* Desk visitor (micro event 35, "A normal workday" in Define Events): $brian measured a power draw on the ceiling
   circuit and wants to open up the vent. Happens once ($flags.brianAskedAboutVent), only while the vent unit runs.
   Shown in the CMD drawer, so no action is spent and there is no exit link. */
<<set $flags.brianAskedAboutVent to true>>
<p>$brian.name stops a few feet from my desk, which for him is practically sitting in my lap. He's holding the multimeter like a candle, both hands, and talking to a spot on the ceiling somewhere above my head.</p>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
	{ who: $brian, text: "Uh. So. The circuit for the ceiling." },
	{ who: $player, text: "What about it?" },
	{ who: $brian, text: "It draws power. When everything's off. I, uh, I turned everything off last night after you left. Lights, the servers, the coffee machine. It was still pulling forty-something watts. Steady. Very steady." },
	{ text: "He pushes his glasses up. His eyes go to the vent grille at the far end of the room and stay there." },
	{ who: $brian, text: "Forty watts is not nothing. It's a lot of watts. For nothing. Could be a bad ballast. Could be somebody's old router up there in the duct. People do that. I could open it up, it's ten minutes. I have a ladder in my car." },
	{ text: "Of course he has a ladder in his car." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<p>He wouldn't ask, either. I know exactly how it would go. He'd climb up, unscrew the grille, point his flashlight at a board that's very obviously mine, because nobody else in this building routes a trace the way I do, and he'd climb back down and say nothing at all. Then he'd go on saying nothing about it, every day, from the desk right underneath it.</p>
<br>
<div id="brian-vent-choice">
	<div>
		<<link "Blame the landlord">>
			<<replace "#brian-vent-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "That's $landlord.callName's air purifier. It's wired into the duct. He made me sign something saying we wouldn't touch it." },
					{ who: $brian, text: "An air purifier. In the duct." },
					{ who: $player, text: "He has allergies. And a lawyer." },
					{ who: $brian, text: "Uh. Okay. That's... that's a really bad way to install an air purifier." },
					{ who: $player, text: "Take it up with him." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>The idea of taking anything up with $landlord.callName visibly ends the conversation. He goes back to his corner, and for the rest of the afternoon he mutters about filter efficiency to his soldering station, which doesn't seem to mind.</p>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<div>
		<<link "Give him a better problem">>
			<<replace "#brian-vent-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "Leave the ceiling to the building. I've got a test board that draws forty watts when it should be drawing four. That one's actually ours." },
					{ who: $brian, text: "Wait. Four? At idle?" },
					{ who: $player, text: "At idle." },
					{ who: $brian, text: "That's... uh. That's terrible. Where is it?" },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>He forgets the ceiling the way a dog forgets a squirrel when somebody throws a ball. By the end of the day he's found the problem, fixed it, written two pages about it nobody asked for, and he hasn't looked up at the vent once.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "Efficiency" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
</div>
